    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA Spectacular and Rare Irish Castle on Approx. 20 Acres of Private Woodlands.Tucked deep within the tranquil beauty of the Irish Midlands, Emmel Castle is one of County Offaly's most striking Historic Estates. A harmonious blend of Medieval fortification and Georgian refinement, this remarkable property includes a 15th-century Tower House and a graceful 17th-Century Country House—set on approximately 20 acres of private woodlands and gardens, in an area renowned for its scenic charm and historic depth.PROPERTY HIGHLIGHTS • Accommodation: Tower House + Country House• Bedrooms: 3+• Reception Rooms: 3• Bathrooms: 3• Land: 20 acres (Woodland, Gardens, Courtyard, Yard, Outbuildings)• Location: 10 mins to Cloughjordan, 1.5 hrs to Dublin, 1 hr to Galway & Shannon Airport• Status: Listed National Monument (SMR)RICH IN HISTORY & CHARACTERFirst constructed around 1450 as a stronghold of the O'Carroll Clan, Emmel Castle once stood among 25 castles under O'Carroll ownership across the region. In 1683, the elegant country house was added by “Long Anthony O'Carroll,” famously close to seven feet tall. Following the Cromwellian conquest, the estate was confiscated but later restored to the family during the monarchy's return—eventually leaving O'Carroll ownership in the 18th century.From the battlements, rising 90 feet, panoramic views stretch across Offaly, Limerick, Clare, Galway, and Tipperary.THE BUILDINGSTower House (15th Century)o Rectangular-plan with circular stair turret (N-E angle)o Pitched slate roof with castellated parapets and bartizanso Stone chimneystacks, loop openings, corbels, mural passageso Defensive machicolations, castellated porcho Historic Great Hall, Music Room, and Art Studioo Master Bedroom, Family Bathroomo All rooms with period fireplaces and latticed windowsCountry House (1683 with 19th-century alterations)o Pitched slate roof, terracotta ridge tiles, rendered chimneystackso Timber sash windows with stucco surroundso Round-headed and square-headed door openings with stained glass, pilasters, fanlightso Elaborate ceiling plasterwork in hallwayo Drawing Room & Living Room with historic fireplaceso Kitchen, Butler's Pantry, Laundry (Garden Level)o Two Double Bedrooms, Two Bathrooms (First Floor)OUTBUILDINGS & FEATURES• Historic stone outbuildings with slate roofs• Walled garden to the south-west of the house• Courtyard accessed by wrought iron gates• Stone and brick outbuilding dated 1883• Ashlar gate piers with carved caps and sweeping boundary walls• Bellcote, date plaques, external stairs, and timber/metal doors with Gothic and Classical detailingLOCATION & LIFESTYLESet in a region steeped in heritage and natural beauty, Emmel Castle offers an exceptional rural lifestyle. The area is ideal for country pursuits including equestrian activities, fishing, shooting, water sports, and hiking.Nearby:• Local shops, traditional pubs, and live music venues• Fine dining within easy reach• Historic attractions and walking trailsDistances:10 mins to Cloughjordan20 mins to Portumna1 hour to Galway & Shannon Airport1.5 hours to Dublin & Dublin Airport"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLower Ground Floor - \n\n\nBanquet Hall - 7.5m x 6.36m\nwith large inglenook fireplace, open to storage area, also beamed ceiling.\n\nInner Hall - 3.88m x 2.64m\n\n\nPlant Room - 3.65m x 3.49m\nwith 2 oil burners.\n\nKitchen - 6.23m x 5.25m\nwith country style kitchen, work island, double Belfast sink, parquet flooring/ flagged flooring.\n\nPantry - 2.29m x 1.60m\nwith shelving\n\nUtility Room - 4.03m x 2.79m\nplumbed for washing machine\n\nBoot Room - 5.95m x 5.64m\nwith inglenook fireplace with solid fuel stove & beamed ceiling.\n\nPrayer Room - 4.23m x 3.86m\nwith concrete floor & stained glass windows.\n\nGround Floor - \n\n\nFamily Room - 15.3m x 5.99m\nwith hardwood flooring, feature cast iron / mahogany fireplace, original shutters, ornate ceiling detail etc.\n\nShower Room - 3.7m x 2.76m\nwith W.C. & H.B. , heated towel rail, shower and timber paneling\n\nInternal hall - 2.21m x 1.05m\nwith stairs to overhead accommodation.\n\n“The Green Room\" - 7.75m x 6.5m\nwith hardwood flooring, wall paneling.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 3.86m x 2.3m\n\n\n“The Red Room\" - 8.64m x 6.53m\nwith inglenook fireplace with limestone surround, beamed ceiling.\n\nBedroom One - 6.35m x 6.02m\nwith cast iron fireplace, hardwood floors.\n\nEnsuite - 2.87m x 1.99m\nwith bath, W.C. & H.B. & heated towel rail (fully tiled).\n\nBedroom Two (Master) - 6.08m x 5.72m\nwith cast iron fireplace, hardwood floors.\n\nEnsuite - 2.84m x 1.71m\nwith bath, W.C. & H.B.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.74m x 2.79m\nwith built-in wardrobe.\n\nSecond Floor - \n\n\nArt Studio / Bedroom Four - 8.48m x 6.47m\nwith hardwood floors, large inglenook fireplace etc.\n\nThird Floor - \n\n\nMusic Room - 8.51m x 6.48m\nwith hardwood floor, double height vaulted ceiling & natural stone walls.\n\nStairs to Battlement - \n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
